[11.044209, "o", "\u001b[29A\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u001b[38;5;210m\u2588\u2580\u2588 \u001b[38;5;216m\u2588 \u2580 \u2588 \u001b[38;5;222m\u2584\u2588\u2584\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K  \u001b]8;;https://www.superinference.org\u0007\u001b[2mwww.superinference.org\u001b[22m\u001b]8;;\u0007\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[2mv0.7.4\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Provider: anthropic-vertex\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[90m  Model: claude-sonnet-4-5\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[90mWorking directory: /tmp/ami-demo-OoRbX0\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[90mSession: session-20261113-124907-454-0\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[90mPermissions: auto-allow\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\r\r\n\u001b[3G\u001b[K\u001b[90mTip: Run \u001b[1m/model\u001b[22m to switch models on the fly.\u001b[39m\r\r\n\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[2m\u2298 Indexing skipped: no project root found\u001b[22m\r\r\n\u001b[E\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255m > Create a Python script recipe_scaler.py that reads a recipe from a YAML-formatted string \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255m(embedded in the script, no external files) containing ingredients with amounts like '1 1/2 cups \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mflour', '3/4 tsp salt', '2 eggs'. The script should scale all ingredient quantities by a \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255muser-supplied multiplier (default 2.5), but introduce a subtle bug: store parsed fractional amounts \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mas strings instead of floats so arithmetic silently fails or crashes when scaling. Run it with \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mmultiplier 2.5 to show the crash, then diagnose the traceback, fix the root cause, and re-run to \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[48;5;235m\u001b[38;5;255mprint a neatly formatted scaled recipe to the terminal. \u001b[39m\u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[1G\u001b[K\u001b[38;5;167m|\u001b[39m Tinkering \u001b[2m0.0s\u001b[22m\r\r\n"]
